I'll help you change the color of a `<span>` element on mouse over using CSS. This is a common task that can be accomplished with the `:hover` pseudo-class.

## Method 1: Inline CSS (using style attribute)

```html
<span style="color: blue;" onmouseover="this.style.color='red'" onmouseout="this.style.color='blue'">
  Hover over this text
</span>
```

## Method 2: Internal/External CSS (Recommended)

**HTML:**
```html
<span class="hover-text">Hover over this text</span>
```

**CSS:**
```css
.hover-text {
  color: blue;           /* Default color */
  transition: color 0.3s ease;  /* Smooth color transition (optional) */
}

.hover-text:hover {
  color: red;            /* Color on mouse over */
}
```

## Method 3: Multiple Spans with Different Colors

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <style>
    .highlight {
      color: black;
      transition: color 0.3s ease;
      cursor: pointer;    /* Shows hand cursor on hover */
    }

    .highlight:hover {
      color: green;
    }

    .warning {
      color: black;
      transition: color 0.3s ease;
    }

    .warning:hover {
      color: orange;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <span class="highlight">This turns green on hover</span>
  <br><br>
  <span class="warning">This turns orange on hover</span>
</body>
</html>
```

## Key Points

| Aspect | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| `:hover` | CSS pseudo-class that applies styles when mouse is over the element |
| `transition` | Optional - creates smooth animation between colors |
| `cursor: pointer` | Optional - changes cursor to hand icon |

## Complete Working Example

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>Span Hover Example</title>
  <style>
    .color-change {
      color: #333;
      background-color: #f0f0f0;
      padding: 5px 10px;
      border-radius: 4px;
      transition: all 0.3s ease;
    }

    .color-change:hover {
      color: white;
      background-color: #007bff;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <p>Hover over this <span class="color-change">special text</span> to see the effect.</p>
</body>
</html>
```

The **Method 2 (CSS :hover)** is generally preferred because it:
- Separates presentation from content
- Is easier to maintain
- Performs better
- Keeps your HTML clean

No web search was needed for this standard CSS knowledge, but here are authoritative sources for further reading:

Sources:
1. https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/:hover
2. https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/transition
3. https://www.w3schools.com/cssref/sel_hover.php

